@tracy/od-design-system
========================

The `systems/` folder in this package is third-party work, copied verbatim from

    OpenDesign — https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design
    Apache License 2.0 (see the accompanying LICENSE)
    Copied on 2026-08-31 (6 files per system); the WHOLE tree copied AGAIN on 2026-09-06 at commit
    3d0d15fc55031e8e6cead709491e7b82565c4dee (about 40 files per system, 4,015 files, 38 MB)

Tracy does NOT modify their content. Every `DESIGN.md`, `tokens.css`, `components.html` and
`manifest.json` is kept exactly as in the original — it is third-party data, and editing it corrupts
the data rather than improving it (docs/references/vocabulary.md §7).

Tracy adds only three things, and all three live outside `systems/`:

  · catalog.json  — an index generated from the 152 manifests, so an agent can choose without reading 152 files
  · slots.json    — the text-slot map of the 152 components.html (scripts/build-od-slots.mjs), so the customer's text lands in the right slot
  · SKILL.md      — how Tracy's agents use this library
  · NOTICE        — this file

NOTHING IS LEFT OUT (decided 31/08, done 06/09). The 31/08 copy took only 6 files per system (DESIGN.md, DESIGN-vi.md,
USAGE.md, components.html, manifest.json, tokens.css) although this line already promised everything — the consequence measured on 05–06/09:
Tracy's skill taught agents that `components.manifest.json`, `preview/*`, `design-tokens.json`, `tailwind-v4.css`,
`source/*` "do not exist", while upstream has all of them. Since 06/09 the `systems/` tree is a verbatim copy of
upstream `design-systems/` at the commit above, containing for each system:

  · DESIGN.md + 17 translations DESIGN-<lang>.md · USAGE.md · manifest.json
  · tokens.css · design-tokens.json · tailwind-v4.css · components.html · components.manifest.json
  · preview/{colors,spacing,typography}.html · source/{evidence.md, tokens.source.json, token-contract.report.json}
  · system/{index.html, kit.html, kit.dark.html, tokens.default.json, artifacts/{landing,deck,poster,email,newsletter,form}.html}
    — the `system/` folder is GENERATED deterministically by upstream's brand engine from a 6-field seed; `kit.dark.html` is
    OpenDesign's generic kit on a dark background using the system's accent colour, NOT a dark mode drawn by the system's author.
  · `_schema/` and `README.md` from the upstream root folder.

Updating from upstream = copy the whole tree again, without picking files. 38 MB next to a 4.4 GB image is negligible.

ABOUT THE BRAND NAMES in the list (`airbnb`, `stripe`, `nike`, `ferrari`…): those packages describe
**a style inspired by** those products — the original titles them exactly that way ("Design
System Inspired by Airbnb"). They are design-description language, not brand assets
being redistributed.

An accompanying TECHNICAL note, not a legal one: a few packages reference the brand's own proprietary
font (`Airbnb Cereal VF` is an example). The font does not ship with this package and is not publicly
downloadable. When building a real interface, replace it with a licensed font — otherwise the page will silently
fall back to the system font and lose exactly what makes that style. Record the font choice in the site's
`<siteID>_brand_guidelines.md`.
